import{_ as n,o,c as i,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 877 | Transcended Ones and Economy | Eliminating Resource Monopoly","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 877 | Transcended Ones and Economy | Eliminating Resource Monopoly","no":877,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Economy","Anti-Monopoly","Resource Monopoly","Myriad-Rank Republicanism"],"related":["47-Anti-Monopoly Law","18-Cultivation-Resource Opening Mechanism","04-Anti-Predationism Core Thesis","876-Hyper-Multiverse Practice of Household-Responsibility Contracting"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0877_模块4-超脱者与经济-资源垄断的杜绝.md","filePath":"en/0877_模块4-超脱者与经济-资源垄断的杜绝.md"}'),t={name:"en/0877_模块4-超脱者与经济-资源垄断的杜绝.md"};function s(r,e,l,h,c,d){return o(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-877-transcended-ones-and-economy-eliminating-resource-monopoly" tabindex="-1">Entry 877 | Transcended Ones and Economy | Eliminating Resource Monopoly <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-877-transcended-ones-and-economy-eliminating-resource-monopoly" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 877 | Transcended Ones and Economy | Eliminating Resource Monopoly&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 47, 18, 04, 876</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-transcended-one-is-strongest-—-therefore-he-is-least-allowed-to-monopolize" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the transcended one is strongest — therefore he is least allowed to monopolize <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-transcended-one-is-strongest-—-therefore-he-is-least-allowed-to-monopolize" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the transcended one is strongest — therefore he is least allowed to monopolize&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s economic monopoly is a natural result: whoever is strongest monopolizes. Spiritual veins held in hand, manuals locked in the vault, secret realms set as private property. Monopolists beautifully call it &quot;transmission,&quot; but essentially it is turning Myriad Ranks&#39; evolutionary resources into the family&#39;s private property. Heng Yuan Zhou must answer: <strong>a transcended one as strong as the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm is himself the greatest monopoly risk source — how does the system prevent him from monopolizing?</strong> This entry explains this question.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the anti-predation axiom directly negates monopoly itself; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires resources belong to Myriad Ranks; the collective ascension axiom requires resources flow to serve the whole; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the monopoly-prevention mechanism be traceable; the law-first axiom requires anti-monopoly laws be self-consistent, not bypassable by the transcended one; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-three-forms-of-monopoly" tabindex="-1">I. Three Forms of Monopoly <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-three-forms-of-monopoly" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Three Forms of Monopoly&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Resource monopoly in the old world has three forms; Heng Yuan Zhou has targeted prevention for each:</p><h3 id="physical-monopoly-holding-spiritual-veins-without-developing" tabindex="-1">Physical monopoly: holding spiritual veins without developing <a class="header-anchor" href="#physical-monopoly-holding-spiritual-veins-without-developing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Physical monopoly: holding spiritual veins without developing&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Old world: great sects occupy the best spiritual veins, only use for their own; outsiders who want to touch are killed;</li><li>Heng Yuan Zhou: spiritual veins belong to Myriad Ranks; any cultivator (including the transcended one) has only usage right, no ownership right. Long-undeveloped veins are automatically withdrawn and reallocated.</li></ul><h3 id="knowledge-monopoly-locking-manuals-in-the-vault" tabindex="-1">Knowledge monopoly: locking manuals in the vault <a class="header-anchor" href="#knowledge-monopoly-locking-manuals-in-the-vault" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Knowledge monopoly: locking manuals in the vault&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Old world: sect manuals are transmitted only within inner sects; outsiders cannot even see them;</li><li>Heng Yuan Zhou: all manuals open network-wide through the Selfless Dao. The transcended one&#39;s insights must be textbook-ified before public (see entries 720, 781). Privately hoarding manuals counts as monopoly behavior.</li></ul><h3 id="channel-monopoly-controlling-secret-realm-entrances" tabindex="-1">Channel monopoly: controlling secret-realm entrances <a class="header-anchor" href="#channel-monopoly-controlling-secret-realm-entrances" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Channel monopoly: controlling secret-realm entrances&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Old world: secret-realm entrances guarded by great sects, pay to enter;</li><li>Heng Yuan Zhou: secret realms are public resources; entrances are uniformly dispatched by the Alaya Network, entry qualification allocated by contribution and need. The transcended one sets no checkpoints, collects no fees.</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-the-transcended-one-is-the-greatest-monopoly-risk" tabindex="-1">II. Why the Transcended One Is the Greatest Monopoly Risk <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-the-transcended-one-is-the-greatest-monopoly-risk" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why the Transcended One Is the Greatest Monopoly Risk&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This is not pleasant to say, but must be said: <strong>the transcended one himself is monopoly&#39;s greatest risk source.</strong></p><p>The reason is simple:</p><ul><li>He is strongest; if he wants to monopolize, no one can stop him;</li><li>He lives longest; he has enough time to build a monopoly system;</li><li>He has the broadest vision; he knows which resources are most valuable;</li><li>He has the most disciples; monopoly can pass down through lineage generation after generation.</li></ul><p>The old world&#39;s Great Emperors, every one was a successful monopolist. They monopolized spiritual veins, monopolized manuals, monopolized secret realms, monopolized the qualification of &quot;who may cultivate.&quot; Then they beautifully called it &quot;transmission.&quot;</p><p>Heng Yuan Zhou cannot, because the transcended one is strong, assume he will not monopolize — <strong>the system must assume he will, then design sufficiently strong prevention.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-five-defense-lines-against-monopoly" tabindex="-1">III. Five Defense Lines Against Monopoly <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-five-defense-lines-against-monopoly" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Five Defense Lines Against Monopoly&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou sets five defense lines against the transcended one&#39;s monopoly:</p><h3 id="line-1-ownership-inviolable" tabindex="-1">Line 1: Ownership inviolable <a class="header-anchor" href="#line-1-ownership-inviolable" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Line 1: Ownership inviolable&quot;">​</a></h3><p>All cultivation resources&#39; ownership belongs to Myriad Ranks, not any individual. The transcended one has only usage and management right, no ownership right. This is a constitutional-level provision (Document 40 Symbiotic Constitution General Outline).</p><h3 id="line-2-alaya-network-multi-layer-supervision" tabindex="-1">Line 2: Alaya Network + Multi-Layer Supervision <a class="header-anchor" href="#line-2-alaya-network-multi-layer-supervision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Line 2: Alaya Network + Multi-Layer Supervision&quot;">​</a></h3><p>All the transcended one&#39;s resource-use behavior leaves traces throughout. The Alaya algorithm automatically detects anomalous patterns:</p><ul><li>Is the number of resources under some transcended one&#39;s name continuously growing?</li><li>Is there &quot;only in, no out&quot; hoarding?</li><li>Are resources being directionally routed to specific groups through lineage relationships?</li></ul><h3 id="line-3-anti-monopoly-law" tabindex="-1">Line 3: Anti-Monopoly Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#line-3-anti-monopoly-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Line 3: Anti-Monopoly Law&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Anti-Monopoly Law (Document 47) expressly stipulates:</p><ul><li>No individual may monopolize more than a certain proportion of public resources;</li><li>Monopoly behavior once discovered, forced breakup + withdrawal + penalty;</li><li>The transcended one violating anti-monopoly law faces a higher penalty standard than ordinary cultivators — because his damage is greater.</li></ul><h3 id="line-4-rotation-system" tabindex="-1">Line 4: Rotation System <a class="header-anchor" href="#line-4-rotation-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Line 4: Rotation System&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The transcended one periodically changes posts and responsible regions, preventing staying in one place too long and forming &quot;territorial consciousness.&quot; Rotation frequency is automatically adjusted by the Alaya Network based on risk assessment.</p><h3 id="line-5-myriad-rank-supervision" tabindex="-1">Line 5: Myriad-Rank Supervision <a class="header-anchor" href="#line-5-myriad-rank-supervision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Line 5: Myriad-Rank Supervision&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Myriad-Rank representatives have the right to question the transcended one&#39;s resource use. If the Myriad-Rank Representative Assembly considers some transcended one under monopoly suspicion, it may open an independent investigation.</p><h2 id="iv-balancing-monopoly-prevention-and-household-responsibility-contracting" tabindex="-1">IV. Balancing Monopoly Prevention and Household-Responsibility Contracting <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-balancing-monopoly-prevention-and-household-responsibility-contracting" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Balancing Monopoly Prevention and Household-Responsibility Contracting&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Household-responsibility contracting (entry 876) gives the transcended one some resource-management right, while anti-monopoly must prevent him from monopolizing — how to balance these two?</p><p>The answer is: <strong>contracting is a time-limited, scope-bounded, assessed responsibility system; monopoly is time-unlimited, scope-unbounded, unconstrained occupation.</strong> The key to system design is strictly confining &quot;contracting&quot; within the responsibility framework:</p><ul><li>Contracting has a contract term, automatically returns at expiration;</li><li>Contracting has a clear scope, may not overstep and expand;</li><li>Contracting has assessment standards, failure returns the contracting right;</li><li>Contracting has Alaya supervision, anomalies automatically alert.</li></ul><p>Contracting is responsibility; monopoly is infringement — the boundary between the two is dead-drawn by the system.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: monopoly locks resources in few people&#39;s hands, wasting Myriad Ranks&#39; evolutionary potential; opening resources is the greatest energy saving</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: monopoly is essentially institutionalized predation — turning public resources into private property</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is the greatest monopolist; he monopolized the Dao, monopolized resources, monopolized the qualification of &quot;who can become strong&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou uses five defense lines to ensure no one — even as strong as the transcended one — can monopolize</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: anti-monopoly faces all Myriad-Rank resource forms, no clan or plane distinction</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: anti-monopoly law, resource lists, and use records all open network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one is strongest, therefore he is least allowed to monopolize. The old world&#39;s Great Emperors monopolized one more than the next; Heng Yuan Zhou uses five defense lines to block all monopoly roads: ownership belongs to Myriad Ranks, Alaya full-process supervision, anti-monopoly law expressly prohibiting it, rotation preventing rooting, Myriad-Rank supervision as backstop. Contracting is responsibility not private property; opening is principle not grace. This is the orthodox definition of eliminating resource monopoly.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/47-反垄断法.html">Entry 47 · Anti-Monopoly Law</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/18-修炼资源开放机制.html">Entry 18 · Cultivation-Resource Opening Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predationism Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/876_模块4-超脱者与经济-联产承包的超多元实践.html">Entry 876 · Hyper-Multiverse Practice of Household-Responsibility Contracting</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',45)])])}const m=n(t,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
